cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  almmr: Tools for Least-Cost Movement Modeling in
  Archaeological Landscapes
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software
  and the dissertation in which the underlying methods were
  developed (see the "references" section below).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jonas
    family-names: Abele
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1540-6202"
repository-code: "https://github.com/j-abele/almmr"
abstract: >-
  Tools for modeling and analyzing least-cost movement and
  accessibility based on digital elevation models (DEMs) and
  friction surfaces, including cost-surface generation,
  Total Passability Landscape Analysis (TPLA), least-cost
  settlement catchment (LCSC) territories, and site-based
  route network (SBR) construction. Example data from the
  Heuneburg region in southwestern Germany are included.
keywords:
  - archaeology
  - least-cost-analysis
  - landscape-archaeology
  - movement-modeling
  - R
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-only
references:
  - type: thesis
    title: 'Der „Fürstensitz“ Heuneburg in seinem regionalen Kontext. Eine landschaftsarchäologische Untersuchung zur Entwicklung hierarchischer Siedlungsstrukturen'
    thesis-type: "Unpublished PhD thesis"
    authors:
      - given-names: Jonas
        family-names: Abele
    institution:
      name: "Universität Tübingen"
    year: 2024
    # doi: "<DOI>"
